course: dictionary
lesson: 12999
title: Clear and special words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Expressly is a formal word, so you will meet it in rules, signs and letters. It is an adverb, which means it tells you how something is done or said. «The sign expressly forbids dogs on the beach.» The sign does not hint or suggest. It says no dogs in plain, direct words.
explain: Expressly can also mean specially, for one particular purpose. «The bag was made expressly for carrying books.» Someone made the bag for that one job and no other. Ask yourself which meaning fits: clearly, or specially.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. «The sign clearly forbids dogs on the beach» still makes sense, so clearly fits. «The bag was made specially for carrying books» also makes sense, so specially fits. Both checks work, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Expressly means clearly and directly, so there is no doubt.
fact: Expressly can also mean specially, for one particular purpose.
fact: «Expressly» is a formal word, so it is common in rules, signs and letters.
fact: «Expressly forbidden» means clearly not allowed, with no doubt about it.
fact: Because expressly is an adverb, it tells you how something is done, like clearly or specially.
exercise: «The sign expressly forbids dogs on the beach.» What does expressly mean here? | Now and then, sometimes | *Clearly and directly, with no doubt | Quietly, behind the sand dunes | Only for dogs
exercise: «The bag was made expressly for carrying books.» What does expressly mean here? | Not at all | *Specially, for one particular purpose | Loudly and in a rush | Very slowly
exercise: «She expressly said no phones at dinner.» Which word is the best swap for expressly? | Quickly | Sadly | *Clearly | Nearly
test: «The letter expressly asked us to reply by Friday.» What does expressly suggest? | Maybe, if we felt like it | *Clearly, so there is no doubt about what to do | Secretly, so nobody else knew | Happily, with a big smile
test: «The tool was designed expressly for cutting wood.» What does expressly mean here? | Badly and carelessly | Many times over | *Specially, for one particular purpose | Quietly and gently
exam: Which word best replaces expressly in «The rules were written expressly for us»? | Partly | Slowly | Loudly | *Specially
